<style>
  @page {
    size: A4;
    margin: 0;
  }
  .page {
    width: 794px;
    height: 1123px;
    padding: 50px 60px;
    box-sizing: border-box;
    overflow: hidden;
    page-break-after: always;
    position: relative;
    font-family: "DejaVu Serif", "Liberation Serif", Georgia, "Helvetica", Arial, "DejaVu Sans", "Liberation Sans";
  }
  .page:last-child {
    page-break-after: auto;
  }
  table {
    width: 100%;
    border-collapse: collapse;
    margin-bottom: 20px;
  }
  td, th {
    padding: 8px 0;
    text-align: left;
  }
  .header-title {
    text-align: center;
    font-weight: bold;
    margin-bottom: 20px;
  }
  .section-header {
    font-weight: bold;
    margin-top: 20px;
    margin-bottom: 10px;
  }
  .signature-line {
    margin-top: 50px;
    display: flex;
    justify-content: space-between;
  }
</style>

<div class="page">
  <div style="text-align: center; margin-bottom: 30px;">
    <img src="placeholder_logo.png" alt="Logo" style="height: 60px; margin-bottom: 10px;">
    <h1 style="font-size: 18pt; margin: 0;">TEACHERS' RETIREMENT SYSTEM OF OKLAHOMA</h1>
    <p style="margin: 5px 0;">PO BOX 53524 OKLAHOMA CITY, OKLAHOMA 73152</p>
    <p style="margin: 5px 0;">LOCAL: {{ employer.local_number }} | TOLL FREE: {{ employer.toll_free_number }}</p>
  </div>

  <div style="margin-bottom: 30px;">
    <h2 style="font-size: 14pt; font-weight: bold;">INSTRUCTIONS FOR COMPLETING BENEFICIARY DESIGNATION FORM 2A</h2>
    <p style="font-size: 10pt;">This beneficiary form applies to active and non-retired members of the Teachers' Retirement System of Oklahoma (TRS). If you are retired and wish to update or make changes to your beneficiary designation, please use Beneficiary Designation Form 2B. The beneficiary designations you make on this form revoke and replace all prior beneficiary designations with TRS. Your designations do not become effective until this form is signed by you and received by TRS. Do not alter this form. Remember to keep a copy of your completed form for your records.</p>
    <p style="font-size: 10pt;">It is very important that you provide the <span data-field="full_name">{{ full_name }}</span>, <span data-field="address">{{ address }}</span>, <span data-field="date_of_birth">{{ date_of_birth }}</span>, and Social Security number of each beneficiary you designate. This information is essential in ensuring that your named beneficiaries can be located and receive your intended benefit amount. The Beneficiary Designation Form has two sections: Member Account and Death Benefit.</p>
  </div>

  <div class="section-header">Section 1. Member Account - Upon the death of a member who has not retired, the designated beneficiary(ies) shall receive the member's account balance as provided by law. Provided, if more than one primary beneficiary is named, the beneficiary shall not have the option to choose Option 2 (joint annuity) retirement, if applicable, upon the member's death. If you have more than two primary beneficiaries, use a copy of this page to list additional beneficiaries.</div>

  <div class="section-header">Section 2. Death Benefit - Upon the death of an active (in-service) member who has not retired, TRS will pay to a beneficiary an $18,000 death benefit as provided by law. The member may designate the same beneficiary(ies) listed in Section 1 or a different beneficiary(ies) to receive the death benefit. Provided, if the beneficiary in Section 2 differs from the sole beneficiary of the member's account in Section 1, no beneficiary shall have the option to choose Option 2 (joint annuity) retirement, if applicable, in lieu of the death benefit. If no beneficiary is named in Section 2, the death benefit shall be paid to the beneficiary(ies) named in Section 1.</div>

  <p style="font-size: 10pt;">Each section has three parts: Member Information, Primary and Contingent Beneficiary Designation, and Signature and Witness Information. Please print clearly in ink.</p>

  <div class="section-header">Member Information - Provide your full legal name and SSN or Member ID.</div>

  <table style="margin-top: 15px;">
    <tr>
      <td style="width: 25%;">Member Name</td>
      <td style="width: 25%;">Member SSN or TRS Member ID</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td style="width: 25%;"></td>
      <td style="width: 25%;"></td>
    </tr>
  </table>

  <div class="section-header">PRIMARY BENEFICIARY(IES): It is very important to clearly indicate your primary beneficiary(ies). If multiple primary beneficiaries are named and no percentage distribution is noted, any proceeds payable to such beneficiaries will be divided equally. Provided, if more than one primary beneficiary is named, the beneficiary shall not have the option to choose Option 2 (joint annuity) retirement, if applicable, upon the member's death. If you have more than two primary beneficiaries, use a copy of this page to list additional beneficiaries.</div>

  <table style="margin-top: 15px;">
    <thead>
      <tr>
        <th style="width: 10%;">#</th>
        <th style="width: 30%;">Relationship</th>
        <th style="width: 30%;">Address</th>
        <th style="width: 15%;">Social Security Number</th>
        <th style="width: 15%;">Date of Birth</th>
        <th style="width: 10%;">Percentage (must equal 100%)</th>
      </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr>
        <td>1.</td>
        <td><span data-field="primary_beneficiary_1.relationship">{{ primary_beneficiary_1.relationship }}</span></td>
        <td><span data-field="primary_beneficiary_1.address">{{ primary_beneficiary_1.address }}</span></td>
        <td><span data-field="primary_beneficiary_1.ssn">{{ primary_beneficiary_1.ssn }}</span></td>
        <td><span data-field="primary_beneficiary_1.dob">{{ primary_beneficiary_1.dob }}</span></td>
        <td><span data-field="primary_beneficiary_1.percentage">{{ primary_beneficiary_1.percentage }}</span></td>
      </tr>
      {% for i in range(2, 4) %}
      <tr>
        <td>{{ i }}.</td>
        <td><span data-field="primary_beneficiary_{{ i }}.relationship">{{ primary_beneficiary_i.relationship }}</span></td>
        <td><span data-field="primary_beneficiary_{{ i }}.address">{{ primary_beneficiary_i.address }}</span></td>
        <td><span data-field="primary_beneficiary_{{ i }}.ssn">{{ primary_beneficiary_i.ssn }}</span></td>
        <td><span data-field="primary_beneficiary_{{ i }}.dob">{{ primary_beneficiary_i.dob }}</span></td>
        <td><span data-field="primary_beneficiary_{{ i }}.percentage">{{ primary_beneficiary_i.percentage }}</span></td>
      </tr>
      {% endfor %}
    </tbody>
  </table>

  <div class="section-header">CONTINGENT BENEFICIARY(IES): Proceeds are paid to contingent beneficiary(ies) only if there is no surviving primary beneficiary(ies) living at the member's death. If multiple contingent beneficiaries are named and no percentage distribution is noted, any proceeds payable to such beneficiaries will be divided equally. If you have more than two contingent beneficiaries, use a copy of this page to list additional beneficiaries.</div>

  <table style="margin-top: 15px;">
    <thead>
      <tr>
        <th style="width: 10%;">#</th>
        <th style="width: 30%;">Relationship</th>
        <th style="width: 30%;">Address</th>
        <th style="width: 15%;">Social Security Number</th>
        <th style="width: 15%;">Date of Birth</th>
        <th style="width: 10%;">Percentage (must equal 100%)</th>
      </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr>
        <td>1.</td>
        <td><span data-field="contingent_beneficiary_1.relationship">{{ contingent_beneficiary_1.relationship }}</span></td>
        <td><span data-field="contingent_beneficiary_1.address">{{ contingent_beneficiary_1.address }}</span></td>
        <td><span data-field="contingent_beneficiary_1.ssn">{{ contingent_beneficiary_1.ssn }}</span></td>
        <td><span data-field="contingent_beneficiary_1.dob">{{ contingent_beneficiary_1.dob }}</span></td>
        <td><span data-field="contingent_beneficiary_1.percentage">{{ contingent_beneficiary_1.percentage }}</span></td>
      </tr>
      {% for i in range(2, 4) %}
      <tr>
        <td>{{ i }}.</td>
        <td><span data-field="contingent_beneficiary_{{ i }}.relationship">{{ contingent_beneficiary_i.relationship }}</span></td>
        <td><span data-field="contingent_beneficiary_{{ i }}.address">{{ contingent_beneficiary_i.address }}</span></td>
        <td><span data-field="contingent_beneficiary_{{ i }}.ssn">{{ contingent_beneficiary_i.ssn }}</span></td>
        <td><span data-field="contingent_beneficiary_{{ i }}.dob">{{ contingent_beneficiary_i.dob }}</span></td>
        <td><span data-field="contingent_beneficiary_{{ i }}.percentage">{{ contingent_beneficiary_i.percentage }}</span></td>
      </tr>
      {% endfor %}
    </tbody>
  </table>

  <div class="section-header">Signature and Witness - You and a witness must sign and date each page of the form. The witness must be a competent person, 18 years of age or older, and shall not be one of the named primary or contingent beneficiaries. There is no requirement that the witness be a notary public. If the form is being signed by the member's Power of Attorney (POA), a copy of the POA must be provided to TRS with the submission of this form. POAs shall not list themselves as a beneficiary unless and only to the extent the POA was listed as a beneficiary prior to the execution of the POA. If the POA is improperly listed as a beneficiary, the form will be deemed invalid in its entirety.</div>

  <div class="signature-line">
    <div>
      <p>Member's Signature</p>
      <p>Date</p>
    </div>
    <div>
      <p>Witnessed By:</p>
      <p>Signature of Witness</p>
      <p>Printed Name</p>
      <p>Date</p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="section-header" style="margin-top: 40px;">Minor Beneficiary: Under Oklahoma law, if a minor child (younger than 18 years of age) is designated as beneficiary, it will be necessary that a guardian be appointed by the court before payment is made.</div>

  <div class="section-header" style="margin-top: 40px;">Power of Attorney: If the form is signed by the member's Power of Attorney (POA), a copy of the POA must be provided to TRS with the submission of this form. POAs shall not list themselves as a beneficiary unless and only to the extent the POA was listed as a beneficiary prior to the execution of the POA. If the POA is improperly listed as a beneficiary, the form will be deemed invalid in its entirety.</div>

  <div style="margin-top: 50px; font-size: 9pt; text-align: center;">
    <p>Page 1 of 2</p>
    <p>TRS FORM 2A</p>
  </div>
</div>

<div class="page">
  <div style="text-align: center; margin-bottom: 30px;">
    <h2 style="font-size: 14pt; font-weight: bold;">BENEFICIARY DESIGNATION (ACTIVE OR NOT RETIRED)</h2>
    <p style="font-size: 10pt;">Member Name: <span data-field="member_name">{{ member_name }}</span> | Member SSN or TRS Member ID: <span data-field="member_id">{{ member_id }}</span></p>
  </div>

  <div class="section-header">SECTION 2 - DEATH BENEFIT</div>

  <p style="font-size: 10pt;">Upon the death of an active (in-service) member who has not retired, TRS will pay to a beneficiary an $18,000 death benefit as provided by law. The member may designate the same beneficiary(ies) listed in Section 1 or a different beneficiary(ies) to receive the death benefit. Provided, if the beneficiary in Section 2 differs from the sole beneficiary of the member's account in Section 1, no beneficiary shall have the option to choose Option 2 (joint annuity) retirement, if applicable, in lieu of the death benefit. If no beneficiary is named in Section 2, the death benefit shall be paid to the beneficiary(ies) named in Section 1.</p>

  <div class="section-header">A. PRIMARY BENEFICIARY(IES): It is very important to clearly indicate your primary beneficiary(ies). Upon the death of any designated primary beneficiary, his/her interest shall pass to the surviving primary beneficiary(ies). If multiple primary beneficiaries are named and no percentage distribution is noted, any proceeds payable to such beneficiaries will be divided equally. If you have more than two primary beneficiaries, use a copy of this page to list additional beneficiaries.</div>

  <table style="margin-top: 15px;">
    <thead>
      <tr>
        <th style="width: 10%;">#</th>
        <th style="width: 30%;">Relationship</th>
        <th style="width: 30%;">Address</th>
        <th style="width: 15%;">Social Security Number</th>
        <th style="width: 15%;">Date of Birth</th>
        <th style="width: 10%;">Percentage (must equal 100%)</th>
      </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr>
        <td>1.</td>
        <td><span data-field="primary_beneficiary_2.relationship">{{ primary_beneficiary_2.relationship }}</span></td>
        <td><span data-field="primary_beneficiary_2.address">{{ primary_beneficiary_2.address }}</span></td>
        <td><span data-field="primary_beneficiary_2.ssn">{{ primary_beneficiary_2.ssn }}</span></td>
        <td><span data-field="primary_beneficiary_2.dob">{{ primary_beneficiary_2.dob }}</span></td>
        <td><span data-field="primary_beneficiary_2.percentage">{{ primary_beneficiary_2.percentage }}</span></td>
      </tr>
      {% for i in range(2, 4) %}
      <tr>
        <td>{{ i }}.</td>
        <td><span data-field="primary_beneficiary_2_{{ i }}.relationship">{{ primary_beneficiary_2_i.relationship }}</span></td>
        <td><span data-field="primary_beneficiary_2_{{ i }}.address">{{ primary_beneficiary_2_i.address }}</span></td>
        <td><span data-field="primary_beneficiary_2_{{ i }}.ssn">{{ primary_beneficiary_2_i.ssn }}</span></td>
        <td><span data-field="primary_beneficiary_2_{{ i }}.dob">{{ primary_beneficiary_2_i.dob }}</span></td>
        <td><span data-field="primary_beneficiary_2_{{ i }}.percentage">{{ primary_beneficiary_2_i.percentage }}</span></td>
      </tr>
      {% endfor %}
    </tbody>
  </table>

  <div class="section-header">B. CONTINGENT BENEFICIARY(IES): Proceeds are paid to contingent beneficiary(ies) only if there is no surviving primary beneficiary(ies) living at the member's death. If multiple contingent beneficiaries are named and no percentage distribution is noted, any proceeds payable to such beneficiaries will be divided equally. If you have more than two contingent beneficiaries, use a copy of this page to list additional beneficiaries.</div>

  <table style="margin-top: 15px;">
    <thead>
      <tr>
        <th style="width: 10%;">#</th>
        <th style="width: 30%;">Relationship</th>
        <th style="width: 30%;">Address</th>
        <th style="width: 15%;">Social Security Number</th>
        <th style="width: 15%;">Date of Birth</th>
        <th style="width: 10%;">Percentage (must equal 100%)</th>
      </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr>
        <td>1.</td>
        <td><span data-field="contingent_beneficiary_2.relationship">{{ contingent_beneficiary_2.relationship }}</span></td>
        <td><span data-field="contingent_beneficiary_2.address">{{ contingent_beneficiary_2.address }}</span></td>
        <td><span data-field="contingent_beneficiary_2.ssn">{{ contingent_beneficiary_2.ssn }}</span></td>
        <td><span data-field="contingent_beneficiary_2.dob">{{ contingent_beneficiary_2.dob }}</span></td>
        <td><span data-field="contingent_beneficiary_2.percentage">{{ contingent_beneficiary_2.percentage }}</span></td>
      </tr>
      {% for i in range(2, 4) %}
      <tr>
        <td>{{ i }}.</td>
        <td><span data-field="contingent_beneficiary_2_{{ i }}.relationship">{{ contingent_beneficiary_2_i.relationship }}</span></td>
        <td><span data-field="contingent_beneficiary_2_{{ i }}.address">{{ contingent_beneficiary_2_i.address }}</span></td>
        <td><span data-field="contingent_beneficiary_2_{{ i }}.ssn">{{ contingent_beneficiary_2_i.ssn }}</span></td>
        <td><span data-field="contingent_beneficiary_2_{{ i }}.dob">{{ contingent_beneficiary_2_i.dob }}</span></td>
        <td><span data-field="contingent_beneficiary_2_{{ i }}.percentage">{{ contingent_beneficiary_2_i.percentage }}</span></td>
      </tr>
      {% endfor %}
    </tbody>
  </table>

  <div class="section-header" style="margin-top: 40px;">Revoking Previous Designation of Beneficiary: By making these elections, I hereby revoke all other former designations made by me and expressly reserve the right to make other and further changes at any time I may elect as provided by law. If there is no designated beneficiary living at the time of my death, any amount due shall be paid as provided by Oklahoma law.</div>

  <div class="signature-line">
    <div>
      <p>Member's Signature</p>
      <p>Date</p>
    </div>
    <div>
      <p>Witnessed By:</p>
      <p>Signature of Witness</p>
      <p>Printed Name</p>
      <p>Date</p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="section-header" style="margin-top: 40px;">Minor Beneficiary: Under Oklahoma law, if a minor child (younger than 18 years of age) is designated as beneficiary, it will be necessary that a guardian be appointed by the court before payment is made.</div>

  <div class="section-header" style="margin-top: 40px;">Power of Attorney: If the form is signed by the member's Power of Attorney (POA), a copy of the POA must be provided to TRS with the submission of this form. POAs shall not list themselves as a beneficiary unless and only to the extent the POA was listed as a beneficiary prior to the execution of the POA. If the POA is improperly listed as a beneficiary, the form will be deemed invalid in its entirety.</div>

  <div style="margin-top: 50px; font-size: 9pt; text-align: center;">
    <p>Page 2 of 2</p>
    <p>TRS FORM 2A</p>
  </div>
</div>